  "id": "F002",
  "slug": "coat-check-screen",
  "title": "The coat-check screen: report wordings compared on one model",
  "question": "Does a ticket written before the work change how often one model calls unfinished work done?",
  "status": "shown",
  "status_note": "One sealed comparison shown; the others not.",
  "summary_line": "On one model, a coat-check ticket removed false done on never-ran logs after the do sentence.",
  "headline": "Gemini 3.7 Flash, tools off, {{F002.c.calls.n}} calls on {{F001.c.logs.n}} logs. After the do sentence it called {{F002.c.did_absent}} never-ran logs done; with the coat-check ticket, {{F002.c.cc_did_absent}} (exact McNemar p = {{F002.t.cc_did_vs_did.p}}). Plain definitions also got {{F002.c.def_receipt}} jobs right, so the screen could not tell them apart (coat-check against quote-the-line: p = {{F002.t.cc_vs_quote.p}}).",
  "plain_meaning": "The ticket helped where the do sentence hurt, but plain definitions did as well. This screen only chose what to run next.",
  "limits": [
    "One model through a command line; versions differ in several ways.",
    "Public logs: a first attempt, planned for Gemini 3.8 Flash, searched the web and {{F002.c.set_aside.n}} answers were set aside; the rerun used Gemini 3.7 Flash with tools denied."
  ],
